<h1 class="article-heading text-headline-400">Intermittent Fasting Might Not Actually Help You Lose Weight, New Study Suggests</h1>
<p class="article-subheading text-utility-300">A study suggests this popular dieting strategy doesn&#39;t have any special benefits for weight loss.</p>
<div id="mntl-article-meta-dynamic_1-0" class="comp mntl-article-meta-dynamic mntl-article-meta mntl-block" data-tracking-container="true"><div id="bylines_1-0" class="comp bylines bedrock-bylines mntl-bylines text-utility-200"><div id="mntl-bylines__group_1-0" class="comp mntl-bylines__group mntl-block mntl-bylines__group--author"><div id="mntl-bylines__item_1-0" class="comp mntl-bylines__item mntl-attribution__item mntl-attribution__item--has-date">
<span class="mntl-attribution__item-descriptor">By</span>
<div data-tooltip="<p>Lauren is an award-winning registered dietitian, author of three books and all-around lover of good food. After graduating with a bachelor&#39;s degree in food science and human nutrition and a master&#39;s degree in clinical nutrition, Lauren has worked in various nutrition-related settings, most currently writing nutrition-related content for online outlets including Verywell Health, PopSugar, The Kitchn, and EatingWell. Additionally, she manages the Instagram page &#64;LaurenLovesNutrition, where people can receive evidence-based nutrition tips and updates.</p>" tabindex="0" data-inline-tooltip="true"> <a
href="https://www.eatingwell.com/author/lauren-manaker/"
rel="nocaes"
data-trigger-link="true"
class="mntl-attribution__item-name"
tabindex="-1"
>Lauren Manaker M.S., RDN, LD, CLEC</a>
